        "math_academy_id": "q-156756",
        "knowledge_point_id": "522fc628-3f81-566b-b7ce-10c75b626c0e",
        "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Related Rate From an Implicitly Defined Curve",
        "problem": "Consider the curve ${e}^{x}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=1.$ Given that $x=x(t),$ $y=y(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=3$ on the curve at the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ find the value of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.",
        "worked_solution": "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{x}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot ({e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, we substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=3,$ $x=0,$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ and solve $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {e}^{0}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) & =0 \\\\ 3+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-1) & =0 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
